{
  "id": "speculative-decoding",
  "title": "Speculative Decoding: Turbocharging LLM Generation",
  "category": "mechanism_deepdive",
  "domain_taxonomy": "neural_attention",
  "hook_tag": "MECHANISM DEEPDIVE",
  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": 1,
      "text": "Every time Claude or Cursor writes code, your H100 GPU wastes 70% of its compute doing absolutely nothing.",
      "visual_focus": "A glowing GPU chip with a flickering red 'IDLE' status bar pulsing above it.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "wastes 70%": "#EF4444"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "GPU",
        "action_verb": "wastes",
        "direct_object": "compute",
        "anchor_word": "wasting",
        "semantic_role": "state_transition"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "grid_memory",
        "title": "THE IDLE PARADOX",
        "sub": "Compute utilization vs. Token generation latency",
        "accent_color": "#38BDF8",
        "params": {
          "grid_title": "Compute Core Grid",
          "active_cell_label": "Active Slot",
          "efficiency_label": "Idle 70%"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "pattern_interrupt_hook",
      "act": 1
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 2,
      "text": "The bottleneck? LLMs generate tokens one by one, like a world-class chef who stops to ask for permission before chopping every single onion.",
      "visual_focus": "A split screen showing a chef frozen in motion, holding a knife over an onion, waiting for a signal.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "one by one": "#F59E0B"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "LLM",
        "action_verb": "stalls",
        "direct_object": "generation",
        "anchor_word": "bottleneck",
        "semantic_role": "causal_link"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "catalog_routing",
        "title": "SEQUENTIAL STALL",
        "sub": "The autoregressive generation bottleneck",
        "accent_color": "#38BDF8",
        "params": {
          "index_label": "Ingredient Index",
          "drawer_a_label": "Salt Drawer",
          "drawer_b_label": "Onion Bin",
          "drawer_c_label": "Spice Shelf"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "villain_bottleneck",
      "act": 2
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 3,
      "text": "Enter Speculative Decoding: a tiny draft model guesses five tokens ahead, while the giant model verifies all five in one single forward pass.",
      "visual_focus": "A small green node firing five rapid pulses into a large blue neural network that validates them simultaneously.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "Speculative Decoding": "#10B981"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Draft Model",
        "action_verb": "guesses",
        "direct_object": "tokens",
        "anchor_word": "verifies",
        "semantic_role": "mechanism_pivot"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "split_flow",
        "title": "PARALLEL VALIDATION",
        "sub": "Drafting vs. Verification cycles",
        "accent_color": "#38BDF8",
        "params": {
          "input_label": "Token Drafts",
          "router_label": "Speculative Router",
          "branch_a_label": "Draft Model",
          "branch_a_sub": "5\u2011token guess",
          "branch_b_label": "Full Model",
          "branch_b_sub": "Batch verify"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "eureka_mechanism",
      "act": 3
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 4,
      "text": "The secret sauce? It pulls matching syntax directly from your repo's AST and git history, shooting draft accuracy up by 40%.",
      "visual_focus": "Code syntax tree nodes glowing as they are mapped from a Git repository into the draft model's input buffer.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "AST": "#38BDF8",
        "git history": "#38BDF8"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Algorithm",
        "action_verb": "extracts",
        "direct_object": "syntax",
        "anchor_word": "accuracy",
        "semantic_role": "optimization_step"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "tree_hierarchy",
        "title": "AST INJECTION",
        "sub": "Context-aware draft generation",
        "accent_color": "#38BDF8",
        "params": {}
      },
      "thriller_role": "technical_secret_sauce",
      "act": 3
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 5,
      "text": "The result? 1,180 tokens per second\u2014a 78% throughput gain over standard PyTorch without losing a single drop of benchmark accuracy.",
      "visual_focus": "A bar chart showing the hero model soaring past Claude 3.5 and GPT-4o with a massive green delta badge.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "1,180 tok/s": "#10B981"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Throughput",
        "action_verb": "surpasses",
        "direct_object": "SOTA",
        "anchor_word": "gain",
        "semantic_role": "empirical_victory"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "comparison_side_by_side",
        "title": "BENCHMARK SHOWDOWN",
        "sub": "Tokens per second performance",
        "accent_color": "#38BDF8",
        "params": {
